    "result_text": "All tests pass (12/12, including the new Cp06 test). \n\n## Summary\n\nI implemented the `initials` field on the owner response, returned as the upper-cased first letters of `firstName` and `lastName`, dot-separated with a trailing dot (e.g. `J.S.`).\n\nTwo changes, following the project's existing pattern for the sibling `displayName` field (which is also a computed, read-only property derived in the MapStruct mapper):\n\n1. **`src/main/resources/openapi.yml`** \u2014 Added an `initials` property to the `Owner` schema (read-only string), so the generated `OwnerDto` exposes the field.\n\n2. **`src/main/java/.../mapper/OwnerMapper.java`** \u2014 Added a `@Mapping` expression on `toOwnerDto` that computes `initials` as `firstName[0].toUpperCase() + \".\" + lastName[0].toUpperCase() + \".\"`.\n\nThis flows through the existing `RespondWithOwner` function unchanged, so `GET /api/owners/{id}` now returns `$.initials` (e.g. `\"john\"` / `\"smith\"` \u2192 `\"J.S.\"`). Since `firstName` and `lastName` are required, non-empty fields in the schema, the substring access is safe.",
